I added the link but unfortunately it does not format it as a link.

@JeZzElLutin comment was already taken into account by reducing to 1500ms.

Thx.

Well, this is indeed a side effect which could lead to a fatal error while executing. This is like pointing to a bad memory zone.

var i;
begin
  while i < 10 do
  begin
    i := i + 1;
    ! i
  end;
end.

This one is also wrong as we cannot assume any default value for i.

This should be the last round of comments for a while!

Constraints
* Please change "<" to "<=" in the first constraint (N).

Cases
* Please add a pair of cases (do not modify the existing cases) to cover simple IF and WHILE. Please insert the pair after the "Simple program" pair. Both cases contain the same program:

var i, j, k;
begin
    ? i;
    ? j;
    ? k;
    if odd i then ! i / j;
    if i = j then ! 999;
    while i < j do
    begin
        i := i + k;
        ! j / i;
    end;
end.

Test inputs: 101, 201, 25
Test output: 0, 1, 1, 1, 1

Validator inputs: 721, 1001, 35
Validator output: 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1

This pair of cases will be able to fix the current coverage issues of "opr 0, 5" (/), "opr 0, 6" (odd) and "opr 0, 7" (=) at the same time.

Thanks.
